ink":"https://github.com/githedgehog/dataplane/commit/70e02bba3128b22c1de3a4fb9f140f718bff2826","commit_subject":"fix(net): end the headers an IP header carries where its datagram ends","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"desihub/desispec","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:18:51Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"2f56a187471a962f1343ea4d54c52e7a723dd668","github_link":"https://github.com/desihub/desispec/commit/2f56a187471a962f1343ea4d54c52e7a723dd668","commit_subject":"Log worker timing for afterburners and zmtl when overlapping tile QA","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"archi-physics/archi","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:18:39Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"abb32022ebc482aa8de5a6d8b3527f80fe76622d","github_link":"https://github.com/archi-physics/archi/commit/abb32022ebc482aa8de5a6d8b3527f80fe76622d","commit_subject":"merge archi_v3 55931da9 into ticket-triage","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"andremichelle/openDAW","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:18:36Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"51134d24f6c30e00e2c0d5a2e7386d66d93d8b59","github_link":"https://github.com/andremichelle/openDAW/commit/51134d24f6c30e00e2c0d5a2e7386d66d93d8b59","commit_subject":"The Mastering panel in the mixer works. Pick a built-in profile (Balanced, Warm, Bright, Punchy) or analyse an audio file as reference, choose a section and Analyse: the mixdown is matched and the project plays mastered from then on, with amount, gain, ceiling, limiter, width and a power switch, live peak, loudness (LUFS short-term and integrated) and correlation meters, and Compare to hear the original at the same loudness. Picking another reference matches again right away. The mastering is attached to the output unit itself, not to its effect chain, and only runs where its device is linked, so the SDK plays such projects unmastered. Compare reaches the engine as a local value that is never stored or synced. The matching curves are limited to ±12 dB, a narrow mix otherwise had its side boosted by 40 dB and more against a wide reference.","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"GMOD/jbrowse-components","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:18:29Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"b7b5c53812cf9f649e146e1877a3f81ef57483f8","github_link":"https://github.com/GMOD/jbrowse-components/commit/b7b5c53812cf9f649e146e1877a3f81ef57483f8","commit_subject":"gnomAD filter-menu figure reshot with the track menu's current rows","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"microsoft/vscode","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:18:12Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"0861b77b3fe8d0d4e2b47c121ef0d2b68fa35992","github_link":"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode/commit/0861b77b3fe8d0d4e2b47c121ef0d2b68fa35992","commit_subject":"Add regression tests for single-item Activity Bar overflow (#345329)","ai_tool":"Copilot"},{"repo_name":"openfootmanager/openfootmanager","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:18:08Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"9612c419930cc69904c7deabd0448e76b3142c9d","github_link":"https://github.com/openfootmanager/openfootmanager/commit/9612c419930cc69904c7deabd0448e76b3142c9d","commit_subject":"fix(engine): every player on the pitch takes a shootout kick in turn","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"lgazo/drawio-mcp-server","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:18:00Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"381021c40563e0682d95c8db6eba50f455509c5e","github_link":"https://github.com/lgazo/drawio-mcp-server/commit/381021c40563e0682d95c8db6eba50f455509c5e","commit_subject":"feat(apps): serve ui://drawio/editor.html shell resource with local editor framing","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"openfootmanager/openfootmanager","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:17:55Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"cce5e6f5ecebeea1275d492b6c97d15a0bfd7f0f","github_link":"https://github.com/openfootmanager/openfootmanager/commit/cce5e6f5ecebeea1275d492b6c97d15a0bfd7f0f","commit_subject":"feat(match): the penalty shootout as a kick sheet","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"rvdbreemen/OTGW-firmware","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-31T16:17:44Z","branch":"dev","com